  "spiritual_reading": "# Spiritual Translation\n\n## ¶5\n\nThe Divine Wisdom proceeding — the great Intellectual of heaven — together with the first state of the regener ating will in its initial vigor, gov erns through the complete ordering of spiritual truths: the full body of revealed doctrine in all its distinct forms, and every derivative understanding that proceeds from it. The seven holy foundational principles upon which all interior perception rests stand imm ov able . The vast expanse of natural cognitions encompasses the whole external mind. The four cardinal tru ths of order extend to every quarter of the mind, up holding the power of divine arrangement in the natural degree, which is the ultimate plane upon which all heavenly states rest as upon their foundation . The five essential faculties proceeding from the Divine Human are those by which the whole mind is established in stable form . The calling - forth of divine truth and the answering reception of the will — together with in destructible wisdom, truth so confirmed it cannot be shattered — these become advers aries to all that opp oses them, and yet it is they who govern all things.\n\n## ¶6\n\nIn the lower degree of the mind, the complete truths of faith and charity stand firm in their fullness. The forms in which these truths present themselves to perception are according to their number . The three essential sustaining principles — love, wisdom, and use — uphold the sphere of spiritual illumination. The remaining three are the external truths with which the Divine Life clothes the regenerating mind; they were best owed in the state of reformation and projected outward together with what is contained within them, made manifest in the forms of the mind. What stands perf ected before the guardian principle at the threshold between interior and exterior states — the one who gov erns passage between degrees by his own sovereign power — these are the three essential divine principles that operate in the midst of human minds. Whoever comes to perce ive them and commits their very life into the keeping of these governing truths is thereby sustained .",
